From 0c0fa9694120d3e3a08b86dcc7ae99c699ebfad6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gregory Thiemonge <gthiemon@redhat.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 15:09:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Fix HAProxy config injection via tls_ciphers field

The tls_ciphers field on listeners and pools was not validated for
control characters, allowing injection of arbitrary HAProxy
configuration directives by embedding spaces or newlines in the cipher
string.

Add input validation at the API layer to reject cipher strings
containing characters outside the set allowed by OpenSSL cipher
strings. Also add a safety check at config generation time to detect
and replace invalid values that may already exist in the database,
falling back to the configured default ciphers.

Addresses OSSA-2026-039 (HAProxy configuration injection leading to
remote code execution in Octavia). Taken verbatim from the merged
stable/2025.1 commit 0c0fa9694120, which applies unchanged to the
2024.1 and 2024.2 code base. Upstream stops at 2025.1: openstack/octavia
has no 2024.2 branch left at all, and the unmaintained/2024.1 backports
are still open, so OSISM carries the fix here.

Must be applied before the L7 redirect patch, which uses the LOG and
validate imports added to jinja_cfg.py here.

Closes-Bug: #2162101
